-- ============================================================================
-- EC1 ASSOCIATE DEEP SEED: Cash Flow & NPV, beginner tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: THE LEDGER. How uploaded rows become years, how a
-- price and an escalator and a deck become the applied price in a row, how
-- the joint venture cascade runs from gross revenue through royalty,
-- depreciation and tax to net cash flow, what a working interest scales and
-- what it does not, and the readings that need no discount rate at all:
-- cumulative cash flow, payback, totals, barrels of oil equivalent and take.
-- It ends before a discount rate is mentioned.
--
-- THE JOINT VENTURE LEDGER MIXES TWO BASES, and that is the shape of the
-- tier. The engine's applyJV scales revenue, costs and depreciation INSIDE
-- the regime, so every row reports gross revenue, volumes, opex, capex and
-- depreciation at FIELD level beside a royalty, a taxable income, a tax and
-- a net cash flow that are the working-interest SHARE. On the teaching field
-- AKATA the 2029 gross revenue is 186032000.00 at every working interest
-- from 100 to 25 percent while the royalty falls from 27904800.00 to
-- 16742880.00 at 60 percent. A reader who scales the wrong lines is wrong
-- by the working interest, in one direction or the other.
--
-- THE TRAP THE TIER IS BUILT ON. Depreciation is a deduction and not a cash
-- flow. It reduces taxable income and therefore tax, and it never appears in
-- net cash flow, which carries the capex it was built from instead. AKATA's
-- default ten-year straight line claims 21000000.00 in 2029 and 25500000.00
-- a year after, 174000000.00 of 255000000.00 capex before the field ends in
-- 2035; the rest is never claimed, and a shorter jv_psc_depr_years of 5
-- moves NPV without moving a single cash flow.
--
-- THE ENGINE FACT THIS TIER OWNS. Government take under joint venture terms
-- is the field pre-take value minus the contractor's SHARE net cash flow,
-- over the pre-take value, so at a working interest below 100 the other
-- partners' share is counted as take: AKATA reads 66.1723 percent at 100
-- and 79.7034 percent at 60. The tier teaches the definition and grades the
-- engine's number as the engine defines it.
--
-- The only numbers that travel from this tier to the next are the ledger
-- rows themselves and the nominal net cash flow column.
-- ============================================================================

values ('cashflow', 'beginner', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-what-a-cash-flow-is","title":"What a Cash Flow Is","lesson_keys":["l01-a-year-is-a-row","l02-what-this-engine-models","l03-what-it-refuses","l04-the-units-that-travel"]},{"key":"m02-from-rows-to-years","title":"From Rows to Years","lesson_keys":["l01-volumes-by-well-and-by-year","l02-dates-years-and-month-indexes","l03-per-well-beats-the-rollup","l04-costs-by-year-and-their-aliases","l05-when-the-file-is-refused"]},{"key":"m03-prices","title":"Prices","lesson_keys":["l01-a-flat-price-and-an-escalator","l02-a-deck-and-the-step-hold","l03-differentials-and-scales","l04-three-streams-one-fiscal-price","l05-the-default-nobody-set"]},{"key":"m04-the-joint-venture-cascade","title":"The Joint Venture Cascade","lesson_keys":["l01-royalty-off-the-top","l02-depreciation-is-not-a-cash-flow","l03-taxable-income-and-tax","l04-net-cash-flow","l05-working-interest-scales-inside"]},{"key":"m05-adding-up","title":"Adding Up","lesson_keys":["l01-cumulative-cash-flow","l02-payback","l03-totals-boe-and-unit-costs","l04-take-without-time"]},{"key":"m06-the-associate-reading","title":"The Associate Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
on conflict (app_slug, tier) do update
  set structure = excluded.structure,
      content_version = excluded.content_version,
      active = true,
      updated_at = now();

delete from public.academy_quiz_questions
 where app_slug = 'cashflow' and tier = 'beginner';

